# Clause evaluations and the time attributed to them. The fixture is a small
# evented speedscope profile: one Split creating three contracts, whose
# observer clause sorts and whose signatory clause reads a field.

# RUN: env PYTHONPATH=%root/src %python -m dpm_trace.cli profile eval %root/tests/fixtures/profile/asset-split.speedscope.json | FileCheck %s

# The engine evaluates a clause once per contract node: three created plus one
# consumed.
# CHECK: DPM evaluation profile
# CHECK: observers evaluated 4x
# CHECK-SAME: interpretation
# CHECK: 3 contract nodes created, 1 consumed

# Ranked by time attributed to the clause, not self time, so the clause that
# called the library function is named rather than the library function.
# CHECK: Where interpretation went
# CHECK: observers @Asset:Asset
# CHECK: signatories @Asset:Asset
# CHECK: is inside a clause evaluated more than once

# The same report from `profile run`, which is where the workflow reads it.
# RUN: env PYTHONPATH=%root/src %python -m dpm_trace.cli profile run --profile %root/tests/fixtures/profile/asset-split.speedscope.json | FileCheck %s --check-prefix VIA

# VIA: DPM evaluation profile
# VIA: observers evaluated 4x

# Neither input is an error worth guessing at.
# RUN: env PYTHONPATH=%root/src not %python -m dpm_trace.cli profile run 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix EMPTY

# EMPTY: error: give a script trace, --profile, or both
